Regarding the error message, try upgrading to the development version of blavaan, which contains some bug fixes. See here:

http://faculty.missouri.edu/~merklee/blavaan/source.html

Regarding computing fit metrics on your own, there are no simple instructions here. You'd have to define the likelihood function, insert posterior parameters into the function, and do some numerical integration over the latent variables. This is tough to get right and is a reason why blavaan does not yet support ordinal variables. The run.jags() command can automatically compute a DIC for you, but it will be a DIC that counts the latent variables as model parameters (which is usually not desired).

Ed

