Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Hi Ed

I am running a change score model, and it is having a problem when converting the model to JAGS code. I found that the problem is that the JAGS code creates this line
31  |  # Inferential covariances
32  |  psi[3,,1] <- lambda[2,4,1]*psi[4,4,1]*NA[NA,NA,NA]

And there it doesnt know what to do with the NAs.

I am attaching an example data set

m2 <- '
## T2-T1
AMCORT2_sc ~ 1*PMCORT2_sc
change1 =~ 1*AMCORT2_sc

change1 ~NA*1
change1 ~~NA*change1

AMCORT2_sc ~~ 0*AMCORT2_sc
AMCORT2_sc ~0*1

change1 ~~ PMCORT2_sc
'

f2 <- bcfa(m2, data=dat,inits="simple",
           adapt=4000, burnin=10000, sample=5000)
Compiling rjags model...
Error : The following error occured when compiling and adapting the model using rjags:
 Error in rjags::jags.model(model, data = dataenv, inits = inits, n.chains = length(runjags.object$end.state),  :
  RUNTIME ERROR:
Compilation error on line 32.
Unknown variable NA
Either supply values for this variable with the data
or define it  on the left hand side of a relation.

Thank you

