Error in blavaan(mod, data, std.lv <http://std.lv> = T, orthogonal = F, group = "group",  :
  blavaan ERROR: 'fa' prior strategy cannot be used with std.lv <http://std.lv>=TRUE.

This is my simulated example:

pop.CFA.A1 <- '
  f1 =~ c(.7,.68)*x1 +
         c(.7,.7)*x2 +
        c(.7,.7)*x3
  f2 =~ c(.7,.7)*x4 +
         c(.7,.7)*x5+
         c(.7,.7)*x6

  f1 ~~ c(.3, .3)*f2

  x1 ~~ c(.51,.32)*x1
  x2 ~~ c(.51,.51)*x2
  x3 ~~ c(.51,.51)*x3
  x4 ~~ c(.51,.51)*x4
  x5 ~~ c(.51,.51)*x5
  x6 ~~ c(.51,.51)*x6

  f1 ~~ c(1,1)*f1
  f2 ~~ c(1,1)*f2

  x1 ~ c(0,.02)*1
  x2 ~ c(0,0)*1
  x3 ~ c(0,0)*1
  x4 ~ c(0,0)*1
  x5 ~ c(0,0)*1
  x6 ~ c(0,0)*1
  '
data <- simulateData(pop.CFA.A1,
               meanstructure = TRUE, sample.nobs = c(500, 500))

mod <- '
 f1 =~ x1 +
       x2 +
       x3
  f2 =~ x4 +
        x5+
        x6
'

bfit  <- bcfa(mod, data, std.lv <http://std.lv> = T, orthogonal=F,
adapt = adp, burnin = brn, cp="fa", group = "group",
sample = 5000)

Is this happening because it is multigroup model?

Thanks again for your help.

